  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Time Zones Look So Strange 🕒🌍🤯",
    "description": "Time zones should be neat 1-hour stripes, but the real map is chaos 🕒 China 🇨🇳 spans five geographical time zones but uses only one, Beijing Time (UTC+8), since 1949, so in far-western Xinjiang shops often open at 10:00 Beijing Time 🌅 Some places are offset by 30 or 45 minutes, like India 🇮🇳 and Nepal 🇳🇵 And the country with the most time zones? France 🇫🇷 with 12, thanks to its overseas territories. Russia and the USA have 11 each 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "France has more time zones than Russia 🤯🇫🇷",
      "What time is it where you are right now? 👇",
      "Which map mystery next? 🗺️"
    ],
